#: admin/settings.php:2492
msgid "Not receiving lead notification emails?"
msgstr "Not receiving lead notification emails?"

#: admin/settings.php:2493
msgid "Default PHP mail() is frequently flagged as spam or dropped by hosts. Configure Custom SMTP under the \"Email & SMTP\" tab using an authenticated provider (e.g. Google Workspace, SendGrid, Amazon SES, Postmark) and send a test email."
msgstr "Default PHP mail() is frequently flagged as spam or dropped by hosts. Configure Custom SMTP under the \"Email & SMTP\" tab using an authenticated provider (e.g. Google Workspace, SendGrid, Amazon SES, Postmark) and send a test email."

#: admin/settings.php:2496
msgid "How does the Submitter Auto-Responder work and which merge tags are supported?"
msgstr "How does the Submitter Auto-Responder work and which merge tags are supported?"

#: admin/settings.php:2497
msgid "When enabled in Form Builder > Settings, the auto-responder dispatches a personalized HTML confirmation email directly to the submitter. It automatically embeds your Brand Logo and replaces dynamic tags: {Name} (submitter name), {Email} (submitter email), {Site_Name} (website title), {Form_Name} (current form title), and {Submission_Date} (timestamp)."
msgstr "When enabled in Form Builder > Settings, the auto-responder dispatches a personalized HTML confirmation email directly to the submitter. It automatically embeds your Brand Logo and replaces dynamic tags: {Name} (submitter name), {Email} (submitter email), {Site_Name} (website title), {Form_Name} (current form title), and {Submission_Date} (timestamp)."

#: admin/settings.php:2500
msgid "How do I connect form submissions to Zapier, Make, or n8n?"
msgstr "How do I connect form submissions to Zapier, Make, or n8n?"

#: admin/settings.php:2501
msgid "In Form Builder > Settings tab, paste your webhook URL into \"Real-Time Outgoing Webhook\". The plugin dispatches non-blocking JSON payloads containing all submitted fields, submission ID, form metadata, and payment transaction details via background HTTP POST."
msgstr "In Form Builder > Settings tab, paste your webhook URL into \"Real-Time Outgoing Webhook\". The plugin dispatches non-blocking JSON payloads containing all submitted fields, submission ID, form metadata, and payment transaction details via background HTTP POST."

#: admin/settings.php:2504
msgid "Are leads saved if email delivery fails?"
msgstr "Are leads saved if email delivery fails?"

#: admin/settings.php:2505
msgid "Yes! All lead submissions are immediately written to your database under \"Lead Generation Form > Captured Leads\" before any email dispatch occurs."
msgstr "Yes! All lead submissions are immediately written to your database under \"Lead Generation Form > Captured Leads\" before any email dispatch occurs."

#: admin/settings.php:2508
msgid "Does page caching break form submissions?"
msgstr "Does page caching break form submissions?"

#: admin/settings.php:2509
msgid "Our forms feature dynamic timing and REST/AJAX handlers. If using aggressive full-page caching (WP Rocket, LiteSpeed, Cloudflare APO), exclude the form page URL from caching to ensure fresh CSRF nonces."
msgstr "Our forms feature dynamic timing and REST/AJAX handlers. If using aggressive full-page caching (WP Rocket, LiteSpeed, Cloudflare APO), exclude the form page URL from caching to ensure fresh CSRF nonces."

#: admin/settings.php:2512
msgid "Where are uploaded files stored and are they protected?"
msgstr "Where are uploaded files stored and are they protected?"

#: admin/settings.php:2513
msgid "Attachments are sanitized and placed inside a dedicated uploads folder (wp-content/uploads/wlgf_uploads/). Direct execution of PHP scripts is strictly blocked via an automatic .htaccess configuration to prevent malicious exploits. Admins can preview files directly from the Leads table with the interactive lightbox."
msgstr "Attachments are sanitized and placed inside a dedicated uploads folder (wp-content/uploads/wlgf_uploads/). Direct execution of PHP scripts is strictly blocked via an automatic .htaccess configuration to prevent malicious exploits. Admins can preview files directly from the Leads table with the interactive lightbox."

#: admin/settings.php:2516
msgid "Does the Digital Signature Pad work on touchscreens and mobile?"
msgstr "Does the Digital Signature Pad work on touchscreens and mobile?"

#: admin/settings.php:2517
msgid "Yes! The signature pad utilizes high-DPI canvas scaling to match your smartphone or tablet retina screen resolution. It captures smooth finger strokes on iPads, iPhones, and Android devices, and automatically stamps the signature onto downloadable vector PDF receipts."
msgstr "Yes! The signature pad utilizes high-DPI canvas scaling to match your smartphone or tablet retina screen resolution. It captures smooth finger strokes on iPads, iPhones, and Android devices, and automatically stamps the signature onto downloadable vector PDF receipts."

#: admin/settings.php:2520
msgid "How does Blacklist \"Silent Drop / Honeypot\" work?"
msgstr "How does Blacklist \"Silent Drop / Honeypot\" work?"

#: admin/settings.php:2521
msgid "\"Silent Drop\" is a stealth defense mechanism. Automated spam bots and phishers receive a deceptive success confirmation on their screen, leading them to believe their submission succeeded. However, the plugin silently discards the payload—no lead is saved in the database, and no emails or webhooks are triggered. This prevents bot operators from detecting blocks and rotating email addresses."
msgstr "\"Silent Drop\" is a stealth defense mechanism. Automated spam bots and phishers receive a deceptive success confirmation on their screen, leading them to believe their submission succeeded. However, the plugin silently discards the payload—no lead is saved in the database, and no emails or webhooks are triggered. This prevents bot operators from detecting blocks and rotating email addresses."

#: admin/settings.php:2524
msgid "Can multiple admin team members receive lead alerts?"
msgstr "Can multiple admin team members receive lead alerts?"

#: admin/settings.php:2525
msgid "Yes! Under \"Email & SMTP\" settings, add comma-separated or newline-separated emails into \"CC Additional Admin Email(s)\". Every valid lead submission will automatically dispatch formatted HTML notifications with these addresses in the RFC-compliant Cc: header across wp_mail, authenticated SMTP, and REST API submissions."
msgstr "Yes! Under \"Email & SMTP\" settings, add comma-separated or newline-separated emails into \"CC Additional Admin Email(s)\". Every valid lead submission will automatically dispatch formatted HTML notifications with these addresses in the RFC-compliant Cc: header across wp_mail, authenticated SMTP, and REST API submissions."

